# `prod` is the shared baseline and is committed. Every other tag is somebody's
# scratch set, and none of them are listed here — they are untracked, not ignored.
#
# There is no rule that would do it. "All of snapshots/ except prod" needs
# `snapshots/*` plus a negation, and git cannot re-include a path whose parent
# directory an earlier pattern excluded — so the negation brings back the `prod`
# directory entry but not the files under it, and a genuinely new baseline (every
# shot of a newly added theme) silently stops appearing in `git status`. That is
# strictly worse than the noise it removes. Both patterns were tried and reverted.
#
# So: `git add -A` after a tagged run will stage somebody's scratch set. Stage the
# paths you mean, or drop the tag directory when you are done with it.
playwright/reports
playwright-build
test-results
